  "limitations": [
    "EXTENSION STRATUM ONLY: these records cover the eight pre-registered extension firms (abbott, baxter, bd, boston_scientific, edwards_lifesciences, stryker, siemens_healthineers, zimmer_biomet) and carry stratum='extension'. They are a separate sample and must never be pooled with the core five in headline numbers.",
    "Record schema is the frozen FETCH_SPEC.md compact schema plus 'stratum'. CT.gov rows use exactly the frozen list of 25 fields=; the compact file drops nothing else from the study object.",
    "Harvest is firm-anchored (CT.gov query.spons / Europe PMC AFF:) and independent of any regulatory record; no milestone-dependent filter was used.",
    "CT.gov date window is applied client-side to first_posted in [2010-01-01, 2025-12-31]; rows with null first_posted are retained. Upstream date strings are kept verbatim (YYYY-MM-DD or YYYY-MM); no day is invented.",
    "Europe PMC date window is server-side, FIRST_PDATE:[2012-01-01 TO 2025-12-31], exactly as frozen.",
    "CT.gov dedup is by nct_id: the first query that returned a study owns the record; additional query strings are appended to api_query joined by ' | ', and a study returned under different firms has its firm keys joined by '+' (sorted).",
    "Europe PMC dedup is by (source, id): first record wins, api_query and source_firm joined with ' | ' and '+' respectively. firm_affiliations comes from the first record and is filtered with the first owning firm's terms only; the (rare) multi-firm rows are counted in counts.by_source.epmc.per_firm_membership.",
    "firm_affiliations matching is case-insensitive word-token equality on the frozen AFF terms, never a bare substring: 'BD' therefore does not match inside a longer word (e.g. 'ABD'), and matching affiliation strings are kept verbatim and de-duplicated in first-seen order. A standalone 'Bd' token in a non-English affiliation string (the French boulevard abbreviation) still matches the 'BD' term; such strings are retained by the frozen matching rule rather than guessed away. An empty list means no affiliation on the retrieved record carried a frozen firm term (counted).",
    "abstract is whitespace-collapsed (no day/HTML invention, HTML entities left as upstream) and truncated to 2000 characters; abstract_truncated marks truncation.",
    "date basis for Europe PMC follows the frozen order firstPublicationDate -> electronicPublicationDate -> firstIndexDate -> pubYear + '-01-01'; date_basis records the source used and 'none' when no date component exists.",
    "Pathological-volume rule: a query whose reported hit count exceeds 15000 is reported and NOT paged (it would otherwise emit a silently partial stratum).",
    "Politeness: User-Agent 'MedRadar-PHOENIX003/1.0 (research; contact chazy11@users.noreply.github.com)', >= 0.35 s between request starts, 3 retries with (1.0, 2.0, 4.0)s backoff; the harvest aborts loudly instead of writing a partial file.",
    "Transport only: responses were requested with Accept-Encoding: gzip and decoded before parsing; server-side query semantics, pagination and record content are identical to an uncompressed request (the smaller wire footprint also reduces load on the shared endpoint).",
